# Security Rules

- Treat all network/client input as untrusted.
- Enforce authentication and authorization at the runtime/service boundary.
- Validate message type, version, size and semantic constraints before processing.
- Never log private keys, tokens, passwords or sensitive credentials.
- Do not hard-code secrets or generate fake credentials as a substitute for configuration.
- Security-sensitive changes require negative tests and documentation updates.
- Preserve fail-closed behavior where required by the architecture.
- Do not weaken cryptographic validation for convenience or tests.
